#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091970 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cb7d8dc0-98eb-53d0-9e48-3b1c2d7f6308" :question/math-academy-id "e-4508" :question/problem "Find a solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=2 \\\\ 4x+3y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091971 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/id #uuid "422d31ad-8caa-5ce2-a0e0-c905fcc2640d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4509" :question/problem "Solve the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 6y-5x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $A\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284734 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efc9c5fb-366e-58cc-800c-cc96a8f541ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284736} {:answer/id #uuid "01755979-0354-5a8c-8358-06db0e668a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284737} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a1d318-b9c1-5dee-a68e-573efd3017fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284738} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ecfbe4-3a59-5c01-b930-32e7ac659265" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284739} {:answer/id #uuid "58ddedb4-aea2-53f6-b4c4-c995257df447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01755979-0354-5a8c-8358-06db0e668a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284737} :answer-field/id #uuid "24ac07c7-8f78-5bfe-8981-b98603a3d774" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "174955d4-f9c8-5173-abe1-fa5e22029d62" :question/math-academy-id "q-102809" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x=1-3y \\\\ 3-4y=2x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x+3y=1 \\\\ -2x-4y=-3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-4)-(-2)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284741 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a62c09b-6d2d-5cbe-82fb-23881dbe8b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284743} {:answer/id #uuid "fe739366-0d06-5d81-900a-b3fa469e5cfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284744} {:answer/id #uuid "36e404a8-b5e0-56ea-bc18-511cd58df34b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284745} {:answer/id #uuid "302f6567-af43-56ac-a05a-0561b14ebd59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284746} {:answer/id #uuid "85b9aebe-294c-573e-82f6-9c8887db1d2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a62c09b-6d2d-5cbe-82fb-23881dbe8b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284743} :answer-field/id #uuid "0af2af69-38b9-5fad-8cf2-7959855a1f5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284742}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33942b97-95c2-5a05-bee1-52e88505e10f" :question/math-academy-id "q-12284" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y=3 \\\\ 2x-y=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74c1eff3-848b-527e-b2eb-31a78b9cdc6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74c1eff3-848b-527e-b2eb-31a78b9cdc6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284750} :answer-field/id #uuid "437fab2a-4840-5e57-84f0-a7ce5da5d04a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284749} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05a70804-9022-598b-940a-594d43a6f796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05a70804-9022-598b-940a-594d43a6f796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284752} :answer-field/id #uuid "746c917a-1444-5ca7-83d2-e1c1beb5c450" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c8de09a-d10c-5c10-a00a-5f3e4740ddf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c8de09a-d10c-5c10-a00a-5f3e4740ddf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284754} :answer-field/id #uuid "7306ddb2-2b1a-5665-ac49-31d6f328b85a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59bf55cf-b55e-56b7-b930-5cbe178314db" :question/math-academy-id "q-320801" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5y=6 \\\\ 2x-y=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $6$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-7$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-5$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $6$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-7$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9252e4f2-9674-582e-b891-6549efc0049c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9252e4f2-9674-582e-b891-6549efc0049c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284757} :answer-field/id #uuid "8778ba95-a77b-55e4-8a77-665b813168e6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284756} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ba1b270-f1c7-500a-9419-e04e449932d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ba1b270-f1c7-500a-9419-e04e449932d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284759} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ce16255-0eef-5d24-966c-82444788326a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284758} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37646cc7-d021-5a1b-9c4c-1673059e10d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37646cc7-d021-5a1b-9c4c-1673059e10d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284761} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7061c7b-909f-5dd5-ba11-8ad9aa46bb55" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3db1b48-5409-5ea4-ac96-413e335ab677" :question/math-academy-id "q-320804" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x=6 \\\\ -3x+4y=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $4$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $6$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-5$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $4$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $6$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-5$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-2\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284762 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8508e9dc-17f3-588c-a4d4-105e6e0627d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284764} {:answer/id #uuid "8ae6135f-e663-518e-9b85-293885d850e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8508e9dc-17f3-588c-a4d4-105e6e0627d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284764} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef8f884f-c987-58b7-9854-595ecd2e6d6f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc6811aa-b7e7-535a-a059-2ea74ea9916c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc6811aa-b7e7-535a-a059-2ea74ea9916c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284767} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce324489-3ef3-5fe5-aaa3-efcdc667656f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c3e9465-747b-5059-b706-27e70d9acba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c3e9465-747b-5059-b706-27e70d9acba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284769} :answer-field/id #uuid "07b2f3be-a17f-553b-b079-5ced5b25ff5a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "997c1f77-09fa-588b-926d-5dbc3c75e96d" :question/math-academy-id "q-320810" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x=y+5 \\\\ x-2=-3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $2$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x-y=5 \\\\ x+3y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284770 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e07c8eab-9079-530a-8d90-dab357ef9a16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284772} {:answer/id #uuid "da7cd9f8-7606-5035-ac45-0a25fc2590d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284773} {:answer/id #uuid "f4171ac5-593b-5eaa-820c-b2896f80fb93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284774} {:answer/id #uuid "1b6c48f2-2b49-5b64-b117-5901ba398177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284775} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd70c31-d552-5b7d-9bfb-413e1e60531b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da7cd9f8-7606-5035-ac45-0a25fc2590d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284773} :answer-field/id #uuid "28b06c62-f990-5be9-a452-5639f051f174" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1683e6f8-f075-57dc-b1d2-9935ccdbc73b" :question/math-academy-id "q-32135" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=-5 \\\\ 2x+3y=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6edb44c1-76ca-5e8f-b7d4-97b421318b65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284779} {:answer/id #uuid "a4896dea-afaf-576b-a304-406bae0e7686" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284780} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa38624-85e8-59a3-beed-01bd9c565ba1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284781} {:answer/id #uuid "ba8f25ce-7926-59d7-9547-59a7487842ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answ